From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:53:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06917/11362] [outer-loop] sk48: L4 SOLVED round 8 (codex,
 first attempt at fresh territory)

Round-8 gpt-5.6-sol session solved L4 on the first attempt. L4
introduces two simultaneously-checked perpendicular chain/guide pairs
(unlike L3's sequential single-chain check) -- both a color-10 and a
color-11 vertical chain must independently satisfy their target
sequence at once. Key subtlety: a block pinned on a vertical segment
behaves differently from an unpinned one during horizontal retraction
(the endpoint passes through a pinned block but pushes an unpinned
one), which is what lets one pair stay complete while the other is
separately restaged.

The winning tail was planned via an offline transition-state search
but the win itself was live-executed: the source agent's own
fresh-environment reproduction gate confirmed reached_level=4, and the
outer loop independently re-verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset()
+ replay via a new resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=4,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: sk48 levels_reproduced 3 -> 4.
reproducible_total_levels 165 -> 166 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
