+    CHECKED perpendicular chain/guide pairs: the color-10 vertical
+    chain at x=23 must see the sequence 9->14, while the color-11
+    vertical chain at x=35 must independently see 8->12 -- both
+    conditions must hold AT ONCE for the win, not sequentially like
+    L3. The rack reads 9,14,8,12 left to right. A key subtlety: the
+    horizontal carrier initially has segments beneath ALL FOUR rack
+    blocks, so retraction is not simple undo -- shortening its reach
+    selectively DECOUPLES already-correct blocks from ones still being
+    staged. A block PINNED on a vertical segment behaves differently
+    from an unpinned one during a horizontal retraction: the endpoint
+    passes THROUGH a pinned block, while an unpinned block gets pushed
+    ahead of it -- this asymmetry is what lets the x=35 pair stay
+    complete while the x=23 pair is separately lifted and restaged.
+    Winning line: a 25-action L4 tail after the banked 81-action L1-L3
+    prefix (106 actions total); levels_completed advanced to 4.
